{"author":{"uri":{"label":"https://itunes.apple.com/us/reviews/id1036689704"}, "name":{"label":"Combatant of gaming"}, "label":""}, "updated":{"label":"2026-09-29T18:03:52-07:00"}, "im:rating":{"label":"5"}, "im:version":{"label":"26.52"}, "id":{"label":"14609157776"}, "title":{"label":"One of my favorite games but I have some questions about the new game"}, "content":{"label":"OK so when I first got this game and learn the ropes I was really enjoying it I built some cool stuff experiments with TNT, and also just explored the open full of biomes world and ever since I first played it I’ve really been having fun with the game whether it’s morning, having build battles with my friends, playing survival, or blowing up my friends base when he kills all of my dogs all my friends dogs. There’s so much to do, however, I have some questions about the new game, Minecraft, dungeons too, even though this is not about the regular game I still have some questions. So to play Minecraft like navigating menus and inventory things I’ve always needed the menu narration because I am the blank player and I currently have my menu narration on for my regular Minecraft on my Xbox and I’m about to play, and I was just wondering, like the first game is there ever gonna be an update that gives us a screen reader a menu narration in and if not, I would just like to know the reason because I practically need my menu narration in order to actually navigate most of the game so if you’re ever coming out or are y’all never gonna be able to add it", "attributes":{"type":"text"}}, "link":{"attributes":{"rel":"related", "href":"https://itunes.apple.com/us/review?id=479516143&type=Purple%20Software"}}, "im:voteSum":{"label":"0"}, "im:contentType":{"attributes":{"term":"Application", "label":"Application"}}, "im:voteCount":{"label":"0"}}], "updated":{"label":"2026-10-15T06:12:12-07:00"}, "rights":{"label":"Copyright 2008 Apple Inc."}, "title":{"label":"iTunes Store: Customer Reviews"}, "icon":{"label":